 days are subject to the state accommodations tax. It does not override local zoning. Cities, counties and HOAs set their own minimum lease terms, and those minimums vary, so a 90-day lease is not automatically permitted where nightly rentals are banned. Mid-term tenants such as traveling nurses, remote workers and October-to-March snowbirds are a common way to cash-flow a property in those zones. Before you count on it, confirm the minimum lease term in that city&rsquo;s ordinance and the HOA covenants for the specific address. Run any address through the analyzer to compare the long-term and mid-term numbers.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What does the long-term rental analyzer calculate?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">For any Grand Strand address you enter, it estimates property value, <a href="/invest/rent-prices/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:underline">market rent</a>, DSCR, cap rate, net operating income, monthly cash flow, cash-on-cash return, and appreciation, and it flags nearby permit activity.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What is DSCR and why does it matter?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Debt-Service Coverage Ratio is net operating income divided by annual debt service. Investor lenders typically look for 1.20 or higher. It tells you whether the rent comfortably covers the loan.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What cap rate is realistic for a Myrtle Beach long-term rental?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">As of July 2026, a Horry County rental bought in the cheaper third of the market returns 4.2 to 7.5 percent a year after costs with a property manager, and 5.1 to 8.8 percent without one. Dividing the same rent by the typical value of every home in the area gives a much lower number, because most of those homes are not rentals. <a href="/invest/rental-returns/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">The rental returns page</a> has the figure for each area.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Are the numbers an appraisal?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">No. They are an actual screening estimate to compare deals quickly. Confirm with comparable sales, inspections, and a licensed agent before making an offer.</p></div></div></section>
